WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.009
Tywin Lannister: Long ago, in the wintry North,
an army of demons emerged from beneath the

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:10.130
icy ground and spread darkness and despair
across the land.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:16.369
Astride their monstrous spiders, flanked by
giants, they wreaked havoc on the innocent,

00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:19.240
slaughtering thousands.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:25.360
All hope was lost until the fearless warriors
of the first Night's Watch drove them back

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:32.899
into the wintry mountains and built a magic
wall to keep them from ever invading again.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:39.320
These stalwart Brothers in black continue
to protect us even to this day from the evils

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.560
that lurk in the shadows.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.980
An absurd lie, a fairy tale, spun by many
a wetnurse in the North.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:56.949
To be sure, a giant wall does exist - a triumph
of engineering, perhaps, but not of "magic".

00:00:56.949 --> 00:01:04.110
As for the Night's Watch, there may have been
a time, centuries ago, when there was prestige

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.710
and honor in the miserable, monastic life
of a Black Brother.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:15.850
But now the Wall has become a glorified penal
colony, full of outcasts, criminals and assorted

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:21.729
ne’er-do-wells.

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:37.070
Sansa Stark: Unlike our southern rivals, the
Stark Kings of Winter didn't forge the North

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:42.939
into one kingdom for glory or gold (there
is little of either here), but to survive.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:49.850
Alone in Westeros, the North remembered when
worse than dragons lay waste to armies.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:55.350
Thousands of years ago, the sun set on the
realms of men, and the Long Night began.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.440
A new race emerged from the ice and snow:
the White Walkers.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:05.299
They demanded no crown, offered no terms,
spared no life, and the dead marched with

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:06.299
them.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:11.910
With humanity facing extinction, a Stark sought
out the Children of the Forest, the most ancient

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:16.849
beings in Westeros, and convinced them to
ally with the men they'd once fought.

00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:22.440
Together, the two races pushed the Walkers
back into the Land of Always Winter and sealed

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:28.730
it off from the Seven Kingdoms with the Wall,
three hundred miles of ice, stone, and earth

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.290
rising nearly seven hundred feet tall.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:36.660
To guard it, they established the Night's
Watch, a brotherhood sworn to defend the living

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.520
from the dead, whose vows erase both titles
and crimes.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:46.220
Viserys Targaryen: After the Long Night, the
North tried to forget it belonged to a continent.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.560
Perhaps through pride, perhaps through sheer
ignorance.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.530
You never can tell with the North.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:55.330
Ygritte: "Swords in the darkness."

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.810
Aye.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:00.120
The black brothers of the Night's Watch are
that at least.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:04.709
When he lies down at night, he can't have
anybody to warm his frozen bed.

00:03:04.709 --> 00:03:08.840
Well, not unless the crows like to "nest"
together.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.099
You think he remembers the stories they told
him then?

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:18.470
About when the White Walkers woke in the Land
of Always Winter and how the Wall and the

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.370
Night's Watch were raised to stop them the
next time?

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.659
Never mind trapping us on the other side?

00:03:25.659 --> 00:03:28.980
We Free Folk have our stories, too.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:35.770
About how one of your king crows found something
cold in the woods with bright blue eyes.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:42.920
How he brought her home, through your wall,
and declared himself "Night's King."

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:49.269
For thirteen years, he and his queen ruled
over his brothers, making sacrifices as black

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:50.580
as their cloaks.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:56.310
Lucky for you southerners, the Free Folk rallied
to a King-Beyond-the-Wall, as we will when

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:01.409
need be, and marched on the ancient castle
he had taken as his own, the Nightfort.

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:07.829
With the help of the Starks, we killed the
demon and cleansed your precious watch.

00:04:07.829 --> 00:04:13.220
And then they thanked us and kicked us back
across the Wall.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.460
As you always have.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:19.329
Jeor Mormont: "Night gathers, and now my watch
begins.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:24.009
It shall not end until my death.

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:29.940
I shall take no wife, hold no lands, father
no children.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:34.260
I shall wear no crowns and win no glory.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.710
I shall live and die at my post.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.880
I am the sword in the darkness.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.690
I am the watcher on the Wall.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:48.260
I am the shield that guards the realms of
men.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:56.750
I pledge my life and honor to the Night's
Watch, for this night and all the nights to

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.290
come."

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:06.940
Legend tells of a winter that lasted a generation,
and of a vast and terrible darkness that fell

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.460
across the land.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.750
It came to be known as the Long Night.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:21.280
In the midst of this darkness, the White Walkers
emerged from the Far North.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:28.520
With their armies of the dead, they waged
war against the living; laying waste to villages

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:34.950
and holdfasts; leaving terror and destruction
in their wake.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:42.620
After years of brutal conflict and unbearable
loss, an alliance of the First Men and the

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.370
Children of the Forest managed to drive the
Walkers and their minions back into the frigid

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:53.110
northern wastelands from whence they came.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:06:00.919
To prevent another invasion, the First Men
erected the Wall, a massive fortification

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:07.610
700 feet in height, stretching from the Frostfang
Mountains, in the west, to the Bay of Seals,

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:08.710
in the east.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:12.570
It was a structure unlike any ever built.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:18.550
Indeed, some maintain it could only have been
completed with the aid of giants, or using

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:23.830
the powerful magic of the ancient Children
of the Forest.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:30.849
Men were required to guard and maintain it,
and thus the Night's Watch was born - a sworn

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:38.590
brotherhood tasked with defending the realms
of men against the dark forces that lay beyond.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:44.130
Upon taking his vows, a Brother of the Night's
Watch serves for life.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:51.389
It is a life of hardship and great sacrifice,
so the oath must not be taken lightly.

00:06:51.389 --> 00:06:55.139
The punishment for desertion is death.

00:06:55.139 --> 00:07:00.710
Maester Luwin: Joining the Night's Watch,
or "taking the black", is a singular honor

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.969
for any northerner.

00:07:02.969 --> 00:07:08.069
For it was in the North, some 8,000 years
ago, that the First Men drove back the White

00:07:08.069 --> 00:07:13.539
Walkers, erected the Wall, and established
the sworn brotherhood that would guard the

00:07:13.539 --> 00:07:17.280
realm and its people from the dangers beyond.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:23.670
Regrettably, the Night's Watch no longer commands
the widespread respect and admiration it once

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.349
did.

00:07:25.349 --> 00:07:29.699
While House Stark and other houses in the
northern regions continue to recognize its

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:34.970
vital importance to the safety and stability
of the realm, this view is not shared by the

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:39.939
powerful houses of the southern kingdoms,
or their subjects.

00:07:39.939 --> 00:07:45.410
Most regard the Watch as a misguided, obsolete
order made up of useless outcasts.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:50.569
Admittedly, the current Night's Watch is a
shadow of its former glory.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:55.330
Samwell Tarly: The maesters don't believe
in prophecy, with good reason.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.161
The Children of the Forest supposedly could
see into the future, yet were surprised by

00:07:59.161 --> 00:08:03.570
the First Men who nearly ended their race
and the Long Night, which nearly ended us

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.319
all.

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:09.000
Some Maesters posit that the Children's magical
sight was invented long after they vanished

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.710
from Westeros by singers hoping to thrill
peasant girls.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.940
Not that most Maesters have much experience
in what does or doesn't do that.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:22.350
The Three-Eyed Raven: War did not come to
Westeros with men.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:26.169
In the dawn of days, the Children of the Forest
fought the giants.

00:08:26.169 --> 00:08:31.870
But neither race sought to destroy the other
or lay claim to the continent.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:37.440
They couldn't; the Children hunted and fought
with dragonglass arrows and spears, and the

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:42.890
giants had hold of the branches they pulled
from trees.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:47.899
Nor could both races fill more than one of
the Seven Kingdoms of today.

00:08:47.899 --> 00:08:54.640
But then the southern deserts coughed up a
new race, the First Men, who had crossed the

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:57.940
Narrow Sea over the Arm of Dorne.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:03.400
The First Men had never seen weirwood, but
the Children had never seen bronze.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:09.890
The dragonglass arrows glanced off the First
Men's shields, and their armor of woven bark

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.650
split beneath the First Men's swords.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:20.220
As the war waged, the children resorted to
the one advantage they had, the magic of their

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.240
Old Gods.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:30.320
Their greenseers enlisted direwolves and snow
bears, cave lions and eagles, mammoths, and

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.320
serpents.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:37.820
In return, the First Men cut down and burned
every weirwood they could find, fearing that

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:42.920
the Children could spy on them through the
faces in the trees.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.420
The Children became desperate.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:51.690
Their greenseers called down the hammer of
waters to break the Arm of Dorne, destroying

00:09:51.690 --> 00:10:00.149
the bridge that men crossed into Westeros,
and to flood the Neck to contain men to the

00:10:00.149 --> 00:10:01.149
south.

00:10:01.149 --> 00:10:02.890
But the First Men would not be stopped.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:08.540
Fearing extinction, the Children combined
their powers for one last spell that would

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:13.190
save their people and their land from the
invaders.

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:18.890
By themselves, the Children were too few to
resist the onslaught, but if they could turn

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:22.820
men's numbers against them...

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:28.790
After hundreds of years of untold death and
destruction, the wisest heads of the Children

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.340
and the First Men finally prevailed.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:37.110
The Children couldn't win this war, and the
First Men didn't want to win, fearing the

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.330
cost of victory.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:47.361
Heroes and rulers on both sides met upon an
isle in the Gods Eye to form the Pact.

00:10:47.361 --> 00:10:53.380
The Children gave up all the lands of Westeros
save for the deep forests, and the First Men

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:58.510
swore that they would no longer cut down the
weirwoods.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:05.290
Thus ended the Dawn Age and began the Age
of Heroes.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.450
Yet after the dawn must come the night.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:14.850
The great evil that the Children unleashed
in the war returned centuries later, and only

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.880
an alliance between the Children and men defeated
it.

